  "worked_solution": "A function $g(x)$ is concave down over an interval $(a,b)$ if ${g}^{\u2033}(x)<0$ for all $x\\in (a,b).$\n\nOn the given graph of $y={g}^{\u2033}(x),$ we can see that ${g}^{\u2033}(x)<0$ on the intervals $(-7,-6)$ and $(2,5).$ \n\nTherefore, the function $g(x)$ is concave down on the intervals $(-7,-6)$ and $(2,5).$",
